{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790419022,"nonce":"T6n2sOzHT4YEpZc2lW5cchyHvyY=","title":"Static members read through a class value, and @:native method names, are not found by name","message":"A class used as a value is its 32-bit type id; `haxe_dynamic_field` / `haxe_reflect_field` return null for it, so `var d:Dynamic = C; d.staticVar`, `Reflect.getProperty(C, \"field\")` (static property getters) and `d.staticMethod()` by name read null instead of the static.\n\nSeparately, a method renamed with `@:native(\"n\")` is registered for by-name calls under its Haxe name only, so `d.n()` on an instance finds nothing.\n\nRows: Issue1492 (both), Issue6871 (static getter/setter via Reflect). Both moved CRASH -\u003e WRONG_ANSWER in c62bfe3bf9, which stopped dereferencing the class id.\n\nDirection: register static fields/methods per class id with the runtime (like haxe_register_method) and resolve by id when the receiver is below 2^32; register @:native methods under the native name too.","files":null}]}